ieee1275: only flag PowerVM on LPARs with hypervisor calls

Any root compatible starting with "IBM," set POWER_VM and
CAN_TRY_CAS_FOR_MORE_MEMORY, which also matches pre-PAPR CHRP RS/6000
machines such as the 43P-150 (compatible "IBM,7043-150", OF TCP99210)
with rmo_top < 512MB (384MB RAM) GRUB calls the non existent method:

  Calling ibm,client-architecture-support from grub...

and uses the PowerVM restricted kernel and initrd claim path. Require
/rtas/ibm,hypertas-functions like Linux prom_init PLATFORM_PSERIES_LPAR.

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

--- a/grub-core/kern/ieee1275/cmain.c
+++ b/grub-core/kern/ieee1275/cmain.c
@@ -49,6 +49,9 @@ grub_ieee1275_find_options (void)
   grub_ieee1275_phandle_t root;
   grub_ieee1275_phandle_t options;
   grub_ieee1275_phandle_t openprom;
+#if defined(__powerpc__)
+  grub_ieee1275_phandle_t rtas;
+#endif
   int rc;
   grub_uint32_t realmode = 0;
   char tmp[256];
@@ -125,7 +128,12 @@ grub_ieee1275_find_options (void)
 	}
 
 #if defined(__powerpc__)
-      if (grub_strncmp (tmp, "IBM,", 4) == 0)
+      /* "IBM," alone also matches pre-PAPR CHRP RS/6000 (e.g. 7043-150), only
+	 PowerVM LPARs have hypervisor calls, as checked by Linux prom_init.  */
+      if (grub_strncmp (tmp, "IBM,", 4) == 0
+	  && grub_ieee1275_finddevice ("/rtas", &rtas) == 0
+	  && grub_ieee1275_get_property_length (rtas, "ibm,hypertas-functions",
+						&actual) == 0)
 	{
 	  grub_ieee1275_set_flag (GRUB_IEEE1275_FLAG_CAN_TRY_CAS_FOR_MORE_MEMORY);
 	  grub_ieee1275_set_flag (GRUB_IEEE1275_FLAG_POWER_VM);
